// tests/fixtures/ambiguous_decls/cycle_indirect.nv
// Phase 0 adversarial fixture: INDIRECT classification cycle (A → B → C → A).
//
// Classifying `Apple` requires classifying `Banana` (call in body).
// Classifying `Banana` requires classifying `Cherry` (call in body).
// Classifying `Cherry` requires classifying `Apple` (call in body).
// Three-node cycle — must produce E0010, not infinite recursion.
//
// --- Why the previous version was wrong ---
// The previous fixture was three structs with mutual field type references
// (Aardvark.peer: Beetle, Beetle.peer: Crane, Crane.peer: Aardvark).
// Field type references don't create classification dependencies — all three
// classified independently as structs. No cycle. Genuine cycles require CALL
// expressions whose callee classifications are mutually dependent.
//
// (EXECUTION_GUIDE.md Phase 0: "construct at least three genuinely different
// cycle shapes … confirm each produces the same well-defined error")
//
// Expected: error E0010 "declaration classification cycle"
// Expected golden: tests/golden/ambiguous_decls/cycle_indirect.json

Apple:
    Banana()

Banana:
    Cherry()

Cherry:
    Apple()
